**Status:** our own feature, in #1 (dedup) and #10 (hardening). Upstream plans message-ID dedup "after multi-leader" (discussion apache/iggy#4373).

Tracks the fork-only dedup feature until upstream provides an equivalent:
- `dedup_window`, with `dedup_header` or `dedup_identity=message_id`;
- missing header refused with 4044;
- window measured in prepare time;
- per-partition metrics.

Evidence: 15/15 acceptance with 0 duplicates; a 20-minute soak at 13.5M keys (81–103 B/key); the U3 crash repro with dedup on gave 0 duplicates.

## Todo
- [ ] Producers set deterministic message IDs (live-producers#149), then consider `dedup_identity=message_id`
- [ ] Re-evaluate when upstream dedup lands
